    "title" : "Avoid Using Arrays as Keys or Elements in Collections",
    "description" : "This rule detects when a method uses arrays as keys in Maps, elements in Sets, or items in Lists where collection inclusion is based on reference equality rather than content equality.",
    "explanation" : "# [Method uses array as basis of collection](http://fb-contrib.sourceforge.net/bugdescriptions.html#ABC_ARRAY_BASED_COLLECTIONS)\n\nThis method passes an array as the key to a Map, element in a Set, or item in a List when\n\t\t\tthe contains method is used on the List. Since arrays do not and cannot override the `equals`\n\t\t\tmethod, collection inclusion is based on the reference's address, which is probably not desired.\n\t\t\tIn the case that this is a TreeMap or TreeSet, consider passing a Comparator to the map's\n\t\t\tconstructor.",
