  {
    "id" : "AWCBR_ARRAY_WRAPPED_CALL_BY_REFERENCE",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Using 1-Element Array to Simulate Call by Reference",
    "description" : "Detects methods that use a one-element array to simulate call by reference behavior.",
    "explanation" : "# [Method uses 1 element array to simulate call by reference](http://fb-contrib.sourceforge.net/bugdescriptions.html#AWCBR_ARRAY_WRAPPED_CALL_BY_REFERENCE)\n\nThis method uses a one-element array to wrap an object that is to be passed to a method as an argument\n\t\t\tto simulate call by pointer ala C++. It is better to define a proper return class type that holds all\n\t\t\tthe relevant information retrieved from the called method.",
