  {
    "id" : "HES_LOCAL_EXECUTOR_SERVICE",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Suspicious Local ExecutorService",
    "description" : "Detects ExecutorService instances created as local variables, which is unusual and potentially problematic.",
    "explanation" : "# [Suspicious Local Executor Service](http://fb-contrib.sourceforge.net/bugdescriptions.html#HES_LOCAL_EXECUTOR_SERVICE)\n\n`ExecutorService`s are typically instantiated as fields so that many tasks can be executed on a controlled number of `Thread`s across many method calls.  Therefore, it is unusual for `ExecutorService`s to be a local variable, where tasks will be added only one time, in the enclosing method. \n\nFurthermore, when a local `ExecutorService` reaches the end of scope and goes up for garbage collection, the internal `Thread`s are not necessarily terminated and can prevent the JVM from ever shutting down.\n\nConsider making this local variable a field and creating a method that will explicitly shut down the `ExecutorService`",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 10,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "HE_USE_OF_UNHASHABLE_CLASS",
    "level" : "Error",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Using Classes Without hashCode() in Hashed Data Structures",
    "description" : "Detects classes that override equals() but do not override hashCode(), which are used in hashed data structures.",
    "explanation" : "# [Use of class without a hashCode() method in a hashed data structure](https://spotbugs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/bugDescriptions.html#HE_USE_OF_UNHASHABLE_CLASS)\n\n A class defines an equals(Object)  method but not a hashCode() method,\nand thus doesn't fulfill the requirement that equal objects have equal hashCodes.\nAn instance of this class is used in a hash data structure, making the need to\nfix this problem of highest importance.",
    "enabled" : false,
