    "id" : "PCAIL_POSSIBLE_CONSTANT_ALLOCATION_IN_LOOP",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Performance",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Constant Object Allocation Inside Loops",
    "description" : "Detects when a method allocates an object inside a loop that is used in a constant way and could be allocated once outside the loop.",
    "explanation" : "# [Method allocates an object that is used in a constant way in a loop](http://fb-contrib.sourceforge.net/bugdescriptions.html#PCAIL_POSSIBLE_CONSTANT_ALLOCATION_IN_LOOP)\n\nThis method allocates an object using the default constructor in a loop, and then\n\t\t\tonly uses it in a quasi-static way. It is never assigned to anything that lives outside\n\t\t\tthe loop, and could potentially be allocated once outside the loop. Often this can be\n\t\t\tachieved by calling a clear() like method in the loop, to reset the state of the object\n\t\t\tin the loop.",
