    "explanation" : "# [Method ignores exceptional return value](https://spotbugs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/bugDescriptions.html#RV_RETURN_VALUE_IGNORED_BAD_PRACTICE)\n\n This method returns a value that is not checked. The return value should be checked\nsince it can indicate an unusual or unexpected function execution. For\nexample, the `File.delete()` method returns false\nif the file could not be successfully deleted (rather than\nthrowing an Exception).\nIf you don't check the result, you won't notice if the method invocation\nsignals unexpected behavior by returning an atypical return value.",
