  {
    "id" : "SCALA_COMMAND_INJECTION",
    "level" : "Error",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "CommandInjection",
    "title" : "Avoid Potential Command Injection in Scala",
    "description" : "Detects usage of system command execution APIs that may be vulnerable to command injection if untrusted input is passed without proper validation or sanitization.",
    "explanation" : "# [Potential Command Injection (Scala)](https://find-sec-bugs.github.io/bugs.htm#SCALA_COMMAND_INJECTION)\n\nThe highlighted API is used to execute a system command. If unfiltered input is passed to this API, it can lead to arbitrary command execution.\n\n    **Vulnerable Code:**  \n\n<pre>def executeCommand(value:String) = Action {\n    val result = value.!\n    Ok(\"Result:\\n\"+result)\n}</pre>\n\n**References**  \n\n[OWASP: Command Injection](https://www.owasp.org/index.php/Command_Injection)  \n\n[OWASP: Top 10 2013-A1-Injection](https://www.owasp.org/index.php/Top_10_2013-A1-Injection)  \n\n[CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)",
